Text 2: Economist Tomas Ruiz agrees that automation raises individual worker productivity, but argues that this productivity gain accrues primarily to firm owners rather than workers, because automation simultaneously expands the pool of available labor by displacing workers from other roles into competition for the remaining jobs, weakening workers'' bargaining position even as output rises.', '[{"key":"A","text":"Ruiz rejects Reyes''s premise that automation increases worker productivity but reaches an opposite conclusion about wages"},{"key":"B","text":"Ruiz accepts Reyes''s premise about productivity but disputes her conclusion by identifying an offsetting labor-market effect"},{"key":"C","text":"Ruiz and Reyes agree on both the mechanism and the outcome of automation''s effect on wages"},{"key":"D","text":"Ruiz argues that automation has no measurable effect on manufacturing wages"}]'::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'The correct answer is B. Ruiz explicitly agrees that automation raises individual worker productivity, matching Reyes''s premise, but he identifies an offsetting effect, displaced workers competing for remaining jobs, that weakens bargaining power and diverts the productivity gains to owners rather than workers. Option A misreads the texts, since Ruiz states he agrees automation raises productivity rather than rejecting that premise. Option C is wrong because the two economists reach opposite conclusions about who benefits from rising output. Option D overreaches, since Ruiz argues wages are affected, just not in the direction Reyes predicts, rather than claiming no effect exists.', '{"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"detail_misread"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"evidence_mismatch"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"inference_overreach"}}'::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 110, false, '{"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-07-08"}'::jsonb, '{"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-07-08","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}'::jsonb);






